Changelog: 27-11-2026 19:59:41

Version 4.9.1.

Changelog: 26-11-2026 20:34:55

Fixed. The mouse wheel changes a list, a number field or a slider only after a click on it. Before, a wheel
turn over a window changed every value the pointer passed. Until the click, the wheel scrolls the page under it.
WheelGuard in widgets.py does it, and create_app() installs it.

Changelog: 26-11-2026 14:03:51

Version 4.9.0.

Changelog: 26-11-2026 12:21:07

Added. log_page.py holds LogPage, the View logs tab of a game manager. Two radio buttons choose the app's log or the
emulator's, emulator.log beside it, which the run wrapper writes. The hint names the file shown, and Clear logs
empties the log shown. applog.EMULATOR_LOG names that file.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 17:44:44

Version 4.8.1.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 15:46:27

Fixed. nexus.py's description names the dashboard Nexus Dashboard for PS5, its new name.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 21:58:22

Version 4.8.0.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 21:31:05

Added. The controller works every app that installs exit_keys, as it works the portal. The d-pad and the left stick move
the focus to the nearest control, and through a list's rows or an open menu first. A presses what has the focus. LB and
RB open the tab before or after, passing over a tab that acts. B still closes a menu, a dialog, then the window. The
touchpad moves the mouse pointer through a uinput mouse of the app's own, at the speed of the portal's Touchpad setting.
The controller still acts only in the app that has had the focus for a moment. The new module processes finds a
program's processes in /proc by their name, with zombies left out, and ends them with SIGKILL together with every
process they started, children first. The game managers' Exit button uses it. The Settings page's message while the
emulator runs now reads "<emulator> is running. Close it first with Exit <emulator>, because it writes its own settings
over the change when it closes."

Changelog: 22-11-2026 20:00:16

Version 4.7.1.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 18:07:36

Fixed. widgets.py.orig, an old copy of widgets.py that nothing used, is gone.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 15:19:54

Fixed. StatusText with a name now shows its dot and name in two colors: green for an ok state, red for any other (owner,
22-11-2026). test_widgets.py checks it.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 15:19:00

Fixed. gamepad.py gave SDL its dummy video and sound drivers and left them in the environment, so a program the app
started got them. Steam started that way crashed on every window. Now they are there only while SDL starts, as in
exit_keys. Both also take out the window class pygame sets. Steam is now always started without these values
(steam_environment()). test_gamepad.py and test_steam.py check it.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 12:25:09

Version 4.7.0.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 11:44:56

Added. steam.signed_in() says whether Steam runs and is signed in. It reads the newest sign-in state in Steam's
connection log. StatusText takes an optional name: the window then shows the name alone with its colored dot, and the
state opens the tooltip. text() still gives the state. test_steam.py and test_widgets.py test both.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 12:04:44

Version 4.6.0.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 11:51:00

Added. same_width() takes a floor: a row's places are at least that wide (the first box's floor), for a card whose
page needs more width than five places do.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 10:50:07

Added. The refresh symbol is drawn muted while it is off (an app that is busy turns it off).

Changelog: 21-11-2026 10:40:50

Added. The card, a template for a small window (card.py, CardWindow; owner, 21-11-2026): the header with the state,
the info symbol and a refresh symbol at the right end of the title row, rows of boxes and pills under it, five on a
row at most and all as wide as the widest, and a width of exactly a full row. RefreshButton is the refresh symbol, of
the info symbol's size and look. AppHeader.add_row() gives a row under the second row; a header without one is as it
was. The info symbol is always filled now, with a white "i": it was outlined, and filled only under the pointer or
with the focus.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 19:26:09

Version 4.5.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 18:49:34

Added. steam: takes_commands, whether the running Steam takes a steam:// address now (the process its pid file names
has Steam's command pipe open, as Steam's own start script tells; both paths are resolved first, since the home
folder is a link on Bazzite, /home to /var/home), and play, which starts a game by its address and waits until it
runs: a Steam that does not run is started and waited for first, and the address is given again, at most three
times, while the game does not come up. For Start game in the managers: Steam started with the game's address came
up and never started the game.

Added. steam: doubles, what is in Steam more than once (how many shortcuts too many per game, for one Steam user),
and put_shortcut leaves one shortcut where it recognizes several: the first is replaced, the others go, the latest
play time kept (owner, 20-11-2026: multiple entries for the same game in Steam).

Changelog: 20-11-2026 13:11:18

Version 4.4.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 03:39:29

Added. builds and builds_dialog: several builds of an emulator side by side, as the version manager of shadPS4's own
launcher (owner, 20-11-2026). builds keeps each build in a folder of its own with a build.json, "current" pointing to
the one in use; installs a download after checking it against its SHA-256 (GitHub's digest, or the one a manager
pins), puts a build in use, deletes one that is not, adds a custom AppImage, tells a replaced member by its size, and
reads a repository's builds from GitHub (github_builds, github_latest; a file without a SHA-256 is left out).
builds_dialog is the window: Installed with Use, Delete and Add, Download with Refresh and Download, the tested build
marked Tested; fill_menu is the menu of a manager's version pill.

